Subject: [PATCH] PC5: two fixes from Mihawk OS (Wine patches 0976 and 0977):
 boolean socket options read back as 1, the cursor clip inside the screen

Mihawk OS 6.0.0-alpha-6's Wine patches 2085 and 2152, unchanged, as Wine
patches 0976 and 0977 (their author kept). A game whose network code
checks a socket option it set against TRUE took it as unset on the
console, and a game in a smaller display mode was told its cursor clip
reached past the screen's sides.
